+
+## Result
+
+The remaining fresh-clone executability defect is closed. Each documented
+`mktemp` template below `$REPO/.temp` now creates that ignored parent at its own
+executable boundary. The two templates below task-scoped `.build` parents were
+audited and already create their immediate parents. The coordinated ten-file
+rotation order and all previously accepted historical/current manifest,
+rollback, compromise, RACI, M2/M5, ownership, and downstream-consumer semantics
+are unchanged.
+
+## Fresh-clone evidence
+
+- A fresh `git clone --no-local --no-hardlinks` began with no `.temp` directory.
+  The deterministic block as documented created it and exited `0`.
+- Two independent builds compared exactly: `relay reproducibility:
+  identical=15/15`.
+- Normalized archive SHA-256:
+  `09014b22e694b1ff4ab664c81d46b3afccd5a973f701cbd4625bfd88c093ab40`.
+- Release-builder manifest SHA-256:
+  `ef5bd8b3cc41ce0e30c026bd088b370faeea30d789a7c6708631330afe8b049d`.
+- Native Darwin/arm64 smoke exited `0` with `pass=17/17`.
+- The native Linux/amd64 request on Darwin/arm64 produced the required gate
+  exit `1`, `native_runner_identity_mismatch`, no artifact observation, and no
+  process start; its enclosing verification block exited `0`.
+- The published coordinated rotation blocks ran from the disposable clone and
+  exited `0`: archive add/get/cmp, two generation/audit cycles, 21 supply-chain
+  and 26 asset-manifest Python tests twice, four Swift manifest tests twice,
+  bundle checks, patch guards, exact staged/applied comparisons, and `relay
+  metadata rotation: changed-files=10/10` all passed. The trial resource and
+  changed metadata remained inside the disposable clone; accepted repository
+  metadata was not rotated.
+
+## Main-tree gates
+
+- Four focused Python suites: exit `0`, 107 tests passed.
+- `swift test --filter RelayAssetManifestTests`: exit `0`, four tests passed.
+- Toolchain positive/missing-input, supply-chain audit, and trusted bundle
+  checks: aggregate exit `0`.
+- `make macos-targets-validate`: exit `0` with only the documented destination
+  and variable-product-name warnings.
+- An initial concurrent `make workspace-generate workspace-validate` attempt
+  collided with the simultaneous macOS validator and exited `2` while both
+  generated the same workspace. After serialization, the exact command exited
+  `0`; workspace scheme and foundation validation passed.
+- Runbook shell syntax: exit `0`, 14/14 blocks.
+- Runbook local links: exit `0`, 32/32.
+- Live concrete board IDs: exit `0`, 44/44.
+- `git diff --check`: exit `0` after documentation and logbook updates.
+- `task-board validate`: process exit `0`; it reported the existing
+  `PARENT_STATUS_MISMATCH` for `EPIC-260715-2lz67t`, whose stored state follows
+  the active child lifecycle rather than a content defect.
+
+## Safety
+
+All execution was rootless and build-only. It did not sign, notarize, attest,
+publish, install, launch an app/provider, access credentials, configure or
+start a VPN, change NetworkExtension preferences, or modify routes, DNS,
+interfaces, or packet filters. No mismatched or remote executable was run.
